ng a Break > Alps"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Relate information about health and healthy habits in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "  Talking About Quantities"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use quantifiers to talk about the quantity or amount of something. <br/>Some quantifiers, like <span class=\"italic\">some</span>, can be used with both count and non-count nouns. You use <span class=\"italic\">any</span> in negative statements and in questions for both count and non-count nouns.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Many</span> is only used with count nouns.   <span class=\"italic\">Much</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">a little</span> are only used with non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Quantifiers</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Count Nouns </span> <br/>teaspoon, cup\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All<br /> Most<br />  Many<br />  Some<br />  Any<br />  A few<br />  A lot of<br />  A couple of<br />  No\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Non-Count Nouns </span> <br/>water, meat\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All <br /> Some <br /> Any <br /> A little <br /> Much <br /> No\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Not all spices are useful. (Non-Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't use much butter.  (Non-Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you give me a little orange juice?  (Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many people here shop at the market.  (Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some pizzas have pepperoni.   (Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Put some water in the pot.  (Non-Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is there any fresh juice? (Non-Count)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you have any lemons?  (Count)"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to focus on  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to concentrate on; to put an emphasis on "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This morning, our show is going to focus on how to make a variety of delicious soups."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you listen to a cooking show."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gourmet   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes food that is difficult to prepare"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love gourmet food! It's delicious!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chef  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who cooks as a profession "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  My compliments to the chef. The meal is excellent."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delicious  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes something that tastes very good "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This soup is delicious!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "salt   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a white crystal you add to food to increase the flavor "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Did you add salt to the soup?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pepper "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a strong spice, often served with salt "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The soup has a bit of pepper."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "soup stock  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the liquid you use as a base for soup"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to prepare the soup stock first."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reduce "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something smaller; to decrease something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Bring the soup to a boil and then reduce the heat. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wonderful  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "excellent; amazing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This soup is wonderful!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud10"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bay leaf "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the leaf of the bay tree used in cooking to add flavor "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Add 6-8 cups of water and a lot of bay leaves to add flavour."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le04ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le04ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of a good recipe you know or find a recipe online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of 5 - 10 ingredients."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For each ingredient, use a quantifier like <span class=\"italic\">a few</span>, <span class=\"italic\">many</span>, etc."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For non-count nouns, choose a count word you can measure, like <span class=\"italic\">a teaspoon of ...</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your recipe with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify the ingredients for a recipe."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express quantities and measurements of ingredients."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain a recipe to my partner in English."}]}], "type": "sena"}